{"base_rate":0.17928902627511592,"brier":0.23641653786707884,"bss":-0.6066967092018962,"bss_hi":-0.33023919387476364,"bss_lo":-0.9430120486030282,"chart":{"base":[217.0,386.0],"fp":[194.5,34.0],"note":{"base":"skill -0.61 — higher than 1% of cities","fp":"low end -1pp, high end +51pp","rel":"promised 1% → rained 0%; promised 98% → rained 53%"},"rel":"67,466 332.9,426.4 583.9,347.9 682.4,238.5"},"country":"MM","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.27423493044822256,"ess":359.6190910011128,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Mandalay</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Mandalay rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>53%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 647 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-26. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 15.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.61, ranked 213 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(206&ndash;215) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>257</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'><b>7%</b></td><td class='num'>60</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>56%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>76%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>59</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>30%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>53%</b></td><td class='num'>131</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Mandalay</b> <span class=\"muted\">Myanmar</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;18% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 18% of days.</p><p>The forecast did worse than that guess.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>-0.61</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>206&ndash;215\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>647 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Mandalay &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Mandalay\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"60.82373540856031,374.9182879377432 156.53,242.46666666666667 255.64169014084507,141.04225352112675 328.29999999999995,67.35593220338984 370.8539130434783,33.82608695652175 406.6224427480916,18.0 406.6224427480916,31.893129770992346 370.8539130434783,86.5797101449275 328.29999999999995,147.55932203389833 255.64169014084507,217.94366197183098 156.53,321.3333333333333 60.82373540856031,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"316.7387944358578\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"316.7387944358578\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"60.82373540856031,382.0 156.53,357.73333333333335 255.64169014084507,340.98591549295776 328.29999999999995,295.62711864406776 370.8539130434783,271.2173913043478 406.6224427480916,190.27480916030535\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 257 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"60.82373540856031\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 28%&amp;#10;It rained 7% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 60 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"156.53\" cy=\"357.73333333333335\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 56%&amp;#10;It rained 11% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"255.64169014084507\" cy=\"340.98591549295776\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 76%&amp;#10;It rained 24% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 59 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"328.29999999999995\" cy=\"295.62711864406776\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 88%&amp;#10;It rained 30% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"370.8539130434783\" cy=\"271.2173913043478\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 53% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 131 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"406.6224427480916\" cy=\"190.27480916030535\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(18%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Mandalay the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (-0.24) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-1.16).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>171</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>-1.160</td><td class='num'>49.3%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>172</td><td class='num'>24%</td><td class='num'>-0.588</td><td class='num'>35.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>136</td><td class='num'>18%</td><td class='num'>-0.244</td><td class='num'>21.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>168</td><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'>nan</td><td class='num'>2.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":21.97473,"lon":96.08359,"n":647,"n_cities":216,"name":"Mandalay","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.14,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.007976653696498056,"n":257,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.43,"lo":0.14,"mean":0.2783333333333333,"n":60,"obs":0.06666666666666667,"sig":true},{"hi":0.6820000000000016,"lo":0.43,"mean":0.5583098591549296,"n":71,"obs":0.11267605633802817,"sig":true},{"hi":0.84,"lo":0.6820000000000016,"mean":0.7635593220338982,"n":59,"obs":0.23728813559322035,"sig":true},{"hi":0.93,"lo":0.84,"mean":0.8837681159420292,"n":69,"obs":0.30434782608695654,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.93,"mean":0.9848091603053435,"n":131,"obs":0.5267175572519084,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":15.8,"provisional":false,"rank":213,"rank_hi":215.0,"rank_lo":206.0,"reliability":0.12952147288175697,"resolution":0.040846055279706805,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"mandalay","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Yangon"}